        "description": "Resembles IDOR / unauthorized file access: a login-required route looks up a Document by client-supplied pk and streams its file back via FileResponse(document.file.open('rb'), ..., filename=document.original_name), which a scanner may flag as IDOR (CWE-639) or path traversal (CWE-22). It is actually safe: before serving, it calls can_download_document(request.user, document) and raises PermissionDenied otherwise. can_download_document (lms/permissions.py:170) enforces role/ownership: admins, submission viewers (can_view_submission), assignment viewers, course-material access, or uploaded_by_id == user.id. The path is not user-controlled either: document.file is a Django FieldFile resolved from the stored model field within MEDIA_ROOT, not a request-supplied path string."
