        "description": "Resembles SQL injection: a user-supplied search string (query, sourced from request.GET.get('q') at the call sites) is interpolated into f-strings ('{field}__icontains') and used to build a DB query, which taint-based scanners may flag as dynamic SQL construction (CWE-89). It is actually safe: it uses the Django ORM, not raw SQL. The query value is passed as the lookup VALUE in Q(**{...: query}), which the ORM always binds as a parameterized argument (never string-concatenated into SQL). The f-string only assembles the field LOOKUP name, and field names come exclusively from the caller-provided fixed allowlist argument (e.g. ['title','body','created_by__username']), not from user input. No user data ever reaches the SQL text."
